
<opts>
<isrc>keybd</isrc>
<iname>INPUT</iname>
<iecho>yes</iecho>
<odest>screen</odest>
<oname>OUTPUT</oname>
<onewl>lf</onewl>
<scrfont>swiss11</scrfont>
<statwin>off</statwin>
<cfmt>~\n</cfmt>
<citer>1</citer>
<cdisp>nolist</cdisp>
<rtype>fmt</rtype>
<rfmt>\n\N\f</rfmt>
<rall>yes</rall>
<starg></starg>
<srpl></srpl>
<scount>1</scount>
<sout>yes</sout>
<nfmt>fixed</nfmt>
<ndec>1</ndec>
<nang>degrees</nang>
<pltng>off</pltng>
<xmax>10.0</xmax>
<xmin>-10.0</xmin>
<ymax>10.0</ymax>
<ymin>-10.0</ymin>
<xintrvls>5</xintrvls>
<yintrvls>5</yintrvls>
<xycells>home,home</xycells>
<cell>
<cname>distributeBushels</cname>
<val>1</val>
<script>    set distributeBushels to 1
    set savedBushels to storedBushels
      in("How many bushels shall be used for seed?",  portionToSeed)
     if(portionToSeed>storedBushels)  {
         set distributeBushels to 0
         set msg to 2
    } else {
        set storedBushels to storedBushels-portionToSeed
        in("How many bushels shall feed the people?", portionToFeed)
        if(portionToFeed>storedBushels) {
             set storedBushels to savedBushels
             set distributeBushels to 0
             set msg to 2
       } else {
           set storedBushels to storedBushels-portionToFeed
           in("How many bushels shall feed the army?",portionToArmy)
           if(portionToArmy>storedBushels) {
                set storedBushels to savedBushels
                set distributeBushels to 0
                set msg to 2
           } else {
                 set storedBushels to storedBushels-portionToArmy
                 set msg to 0
           }
       }
   }
}</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>harvest</cname>
<val>39411</val>
<script>set harvest sig(population-150)*(1.30+rand()) * portionToSeed
</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>home</cname>
<text>King allows the user to pretend to govern a kingdom.  Success is a growing population and grain reserves.  Failure is a dwindling population and famine.

The variables controlled by the King are:  Bushels for food, bushels to plant, bushels for defense....allocation of the harvest to diferent purposes.

Position to this cell and select Execute from the Special menu to start this program.</text>
<script>set NumDecX to 0
set storedBushels 50000
set penaltyFlag to 0
set population 500
set harvest 10000
set msg to 0
set year to 0
while(not eof) {
      set year to year+1
      msg0[msg]()
      if(distributeBushels! =1) { # valid input
            if(portionToArmy&lt;2000) {
                set penaltyFlag to 1+penaltyFlag
            } else {
                if(penaltyFlag>0) {
                      set penaltyFlag to penaltyFlag-1
                } #endif
            } #endif
            harvest!
            population!
           if( population!&lt;=0) {
                set msg to 5
           } elseif(penaltyFlag>5*rand()) {
                 set  penaltyFlag to 0
                 set harvest to harvest/2
                 set msg to 1
           } elseif(10*rand()>9) {
                set msg to 4
                set harvest to 0.667*harvest
           } elseif(10*rand()>9) {
                set msg to 3
                set population to 9*population/10
           } #endif
           set storedBushels to storedBushels+harvest     
      } else {
           set harvest to 0
      } #endif
} #endwh
</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>msg</cname>
<val>0</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>msg0</cname>
<script>out("\nOh King, it is year ",year," of your reign.")
out("The yearly census reveals that you have ",population," loyal subjects", "  Your subjects have produced ",harvest," bushels of wheat this year, giving a total storage of ",storedBushels,"  bushels\f")
</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>msg1</cname>
<script>out("\nSire, it is year ",year," of your reign.")
out("Bandits have attacked the grain warehouse.  Much grain was taken.  Some was burned.  Luckily, half of the harvest was saved.")
out("You have ",population,"frightened subjects", "  Your subjects managed to save ",storedBushels, " bushels of grain\f")

</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>msg2</cname>
<script>out("\nYour allocation plan is arithmetically impossible master.  Perhaps we should try again?")
out("\nYou have ",population," subjects", "  Your total grain storage is  ",storedBushels,"  bushels.\f")
set year to year-1</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>msg3</cname>
<script>out("\nSire, it is year ",year," of your reign.")
out("Your subjects have been decimated by a plague.")
out("You have ",population," subjects", "  Your total grain storage is  ",storedBushels," bushels.\f")
</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>msg4</cname>
<script>out("\nSire, it is year ",year," of your reign.")
out("\nA virus has wiped out a third  of your grain harvest.")
out("\nYou have ",population," subjects", "  Your total grain storage is  ",storedBushels, " bushels.\f")
</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>msg5</cname>
<script>out("\nSire, it is year ",year," of your reign")
out("\nYou have starved your subjects to death.")
out("\nYou now rule over a cemetary")
exit
</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>penaltyFlag</cname>
<val>0</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>population</cname>
<val>325</val>
<script>population*(1.05*portionToFeed/(population*60)-0.08)</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>portionToArmy</cname>
<val>2000</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>portionToFeed</cname>
<val>20000</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>portionToSeed</cname>
<val>20000</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>savedBushels</cname>
<val>47411</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>storedBushels</cname>
<val>47411</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>year</cname>
<val>2</val></cell></eof>